# SPA fallback: client-side routing means every path has to reach index.html.
#
# A real file always wins over this rule, so /assets/<hash>.js is served as
# JavaScript for as long as that deployment is live. A chunk from an OLDER
# deployment no longer exists, and the request falls through to here — the
# browser asks for a module and gets HTML, which is the
# "Failed to fetch dynamically imported module" error a tab left open across a
# deploy runs into. Pages does not support 404 in this file, so the recovery is
# client-side: src/lib/stale-deploy.ts reloads the tab once to pick up the new
# index.html.
